playground-output/

# Local agent tooling (Claude Code skills). Not project code — installed per
# machine, third-party content with its own licences. Delete this line if the
# team decides to share a skill set through the repo.
.claude/

# Unattended verification: generated evidence and the live-log pointer.
#
# ⚠️ scripts/reports/ is ignored for a load-bearing reason, not tidiness: `deployment-integrity.mjs`
# asserts "the working tree is clean — what is deployed can be named by a commit hash". Untracked
# report output makes that check red on every run, so the framework would fail a real verification by
# producing its own output. The runs are still on disk to read; they are simply not repository state.
scripts/logs/
scripts/reports/

# ── P-8 Phase 4 tracking fixtures ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated by docs/review/p8/tracking-fixtures.mjs from scene-people.jpg plus the boxes the DEPLOYED
# model returns. ⚠️ The clips are deliberately NOT committed: they are ~1 MB of derived binary that
# any machine can rebuild in twenty seconds, and a committed video is a thing that silently stops
# matching the generator that claims to produce it. `ground-truth.json` IS committed — it is the
# authored contract the assertions are written against, and it must be reviewable in a diff.
infra/docker/fixtures/media/tracking/*.mp4
infra/docker/fixtures/media/tracking/*.png
infra/docker/fixtures/media/tracking/frames/

# ── P-8.5 validation dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated by `node tools/dataset/generate.mjs --verify` from scene-people.jpg plus the boxes the
# DEPLOYED model returns. ⚠️ Reproducible by construction and ~22 MB, so the *recipe* is committed
# (tools/dataset/) and the bytes are not — the same decision the tracking fixtures made.
#
# ⭐ `manifest.json` IS committed: it holds the MEASURED ground truth every test asserts against, and
# a suite whose expectations regenerate themselves is a suite that can never fail.
infra/docker/fixtures/media/validation/*.mp4
infra/docker/fixtures/media/validation/*.png
infra/docker/fixtures/media/validation/frames/
# ⭐ **One exception, and it earns it.** The rule above works because an authored clip regenerates
# from `tools/dataset/generate.mjs` in seconds. This one does not: it is a pan across an external
# CC0 photograph that has to be fetched, resized and rendered, and it is the **only** clip in this
# repository from which the deployed detector returns a carriable object. Every object-association
# number published in `docs/validation/OBJECT_ASSOCIATION.md` was measured on these exact bytes, and
# a verification whose stimulus cannot be reproduced is a verification nobody can check.
# ⚠️ CC0, so committing it carries no licensing obligation — provenance is in the manifest entry.
!infra/docker/fixtures/media/validation/carried-objects.mp4
# The duration/size ladder — hundreds of MB, generated on demand for a performance run.
infra/docker/fixtures/media/validation/large/

# P-8.5 validation and browser-certification artefacts (runs, screenshots, traces).
artifacts/
tools/e2e-browser/artifacts/

# Release-soak run artefacts (JSONL streams, several MB per run). The harness is tracked; its
# output is not — SOAK_REPORT.md and its siblings carry the conclusions into the repo.
.soak*/
.soak-real.mp4
